{"id":47300,"ord":12,"n_segments":152,"prev":47299,"next":47301,"doc":{"id":"61125","title":"61125_Teddy Bunn oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Theodore Leroy Bunn","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/61125/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=61125"},"chapter":"Harlem, the Cotton Club and Duke Ellington","title":"Staying on with Ellington; Fred Guy and the guitar role","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Duke kept him after his first night; Fred Guy played rhythm banjo while Bunn took fills and solos.","period":"c. 1929","year_from":1929,"year_to":1929,"words":148,"start":[17,16],"end":[19,5],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=61125#s47300","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Duke Ellington Orchestra","focus":1,"leader":"Duke Ellington"}]},"people":[{"name":"Fred Guy","qid":"Q277998","n":5},{"name":"Duke Ellington","qid":"Q4030","n":1}],"story":{"theme":2,"theme_name":"Duke Ellington and his orchestra, as others knew them","community":5,"community_name":"Duke Ellington: the band, the man, his men","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":17,"b":16,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Well, then, when did Duke ask you to actually play with the orchestra?"},{"p":18,"b":0,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Huh? I kept it when I had that job that night."},{"p":18,"b":1,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":18,"b":2,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"They kept me there after I went over so nice."},{"p":18,"b":3,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":18,"b":4,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"They kept me there."},{"p":18,"b":5,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"But then, was Fred Guy playing also?"},{"p":18,"b":6,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Fred Guy was drummer. I mean --"},{"p":18,"b":7,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Rhythm."},{"p":18,"b":8,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Rhythm."},{"p":18,"b":9,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Right."},{"p":18,"b":10,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"He played guitar."},{"p":18,"b":11,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"And banjo, too."},{"p":18,"b":12,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"And banjo."},{"p":18,"b":13,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"And then, so for awhile you and Fred Guy were both playing guitar."},{"p":18,"b":14,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":18,"b":15,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"At the same time. Is that right?"},{"p":18,"b":16,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"No."},{"p":18,"b":17,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"No."},{"p":18,"b":18,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Not unless he sat in with me and I forgot that."},{"p":18,"b":19,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":18,"b":20,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"But I don't know -- Fred Guy was playing"},{"p":19,"b":0,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Oh, I see. So Fred Guy was playing the rhythm banjo."},{"p":19,"b":1,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah, the rhythm banjo."},{"p":19,"b":2,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"And you were taking the short -- the fills and the solos."},{"p":19,"b":3,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"The fills and the solos."},{"p":19,"b":4,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"And kicking things off."},{"p":19,"b":5,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"That's right, yeah."}]}